AureliaCode adaptation, which does not replace the upstream workflow:

- Invocation is only `/untangle-codebase [optional area]`.
- `disable-model-invocation: true` stays, so the model does not run it on its own.
- Installing these files does not start a refactor and does not edit a codebase.
- The user may name additions: refactor only, refactor plus comments, refactor
  plus tests, or both. With no choice, the skill asks. Tests are not deleted
  unless the user opts in.
- The decision log and a proposed plan are shown, and the user confirms them,
  before any destructive edit.

The comments and tests descriptions, the hidden-link / needless-link / surplus
categories, the special-case log, the redesign step, and the end-to-end check
are the upstream workflow.
